-- title:
--   Frobenius squared acts by p² on prime-to-p toric torsion
-- statement:
--   Fix natural numbers $N_0$ and $p$ with $p$ prime, $N_0$ nonzero and $p \nmid N_0$. Let $A$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbf Q} =$ `AlgebraicClosure ℚ` lying over $p$, in the sense that $p$ is a non-unit of $A$, let $\Lambda$ be a `LevelData` for $(N_0,p,A)$ — a scheme $X$ over the base of $p$ together with a relative group law, identifications of $J_0(N_0)(\overline{\mathbf Q})$ with sections over the generic point and of the special-fibre points over the residue field of $A$ with sections over the reduction point — satisfying `IsJacobian` (abelian-scheme property bundle, commutativity, additivity and Galois equivariance of the two point parametrisations, compatibility of reduction of points, and realisation of every Hecke operator by an endomorphism over the base), and let $O$ be a `JZeroNeronObjectAtP` for these data, i.e. a smooth separated surjective group object $G \to \mathrm{base}(p)$ of finite type with preconnected fibres, equipped with an additive Galois-equivariant parametrisation of $J_0(N_0p)(\overline{\mathbf Q})$, Hecke endomorphisms, flat surjective multiplication-by-$n$ maps, properness of the generic fibre, and toric data. Assume $(hIU)$: for every $m$ coprime to $p$, every $\sigma$ in the image of the inertia subgroup of $A$ over $\mathbf Q$ and every $x$ in the $m$-torsion of $J_0(N_0p)$, the difference $\sigma \cdot x - x$ lies in $O.\mathrm{toricPts}\,m$, the subgroup generated by the range of $O.\mathrm{toricPoint}\,m$. Let $m > 0$ be coprime to $p$. Then for every $\mathbf Q$-algebra automorphism $\sigma$ of $\overline{\mathbf Q}$ which is a Frobenius at $p$ for $A$ — that is, $\sigma$ lies in the decomposition subgroup of $A$ and acts on the residue field of $A$ by $y \mapsto y^p$ — and every $x \in O.\mathrm{toricPts}\,m$, one has $\sigma \cdot \sigma \cdot x = p^2 \cdot x$.
--
--   This records the fact that the toric part of the Néron model of $J_0(N_0p)$ at $p$ splits over the quadratic extension of the residue field, so that the square of a Frobenius element acts on the prime-to-$p$ toric torsion by the scalar $p^2$; this is the Frobenius-eigenvalue input to the local analysis at $p$ used in level lowering. It is used in the construction of the ordinary local data attached to $O$.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_JZeroNeronObjectAtP_smul_smul_eq_of_isFrobeniusAt_of_mem_toricPts_of_forall_smul_sub_mem_toricPts.lean

